 needs work beyond the initial scope, that should be discussed rather than hidden inside an assumed standard estimate. The decision is based on the actual cabinet and the findings on your site.</p><p>Our London service covers business locations including Camden, Hackney, Barnet, Westminster and Southwark, with urgent calls accepted throughout the day and night. Contact 07983 759320 and provide the postcode, access arrangements and a number for the responsible manager. Keep alarm records or recent maintenance details available and follow your stock handling procedures while cooling is interrupted. For dedicated equipment, the services grid links to freezer, display cabinet and cold room repair pages with more specific information. Ask about the checks completed after the work and the warranty that accompanies the repair. We aim to make the findings understandable so your team knows what has been addressed and what still needs attention.</p><h3>Useful symptoms to report for a business fridge</h3><ul><li>Cabinet temperature rising gradually: the pattern may involve ventilation, sealing or cooling performance, so note when the problem began and whether it becomes worse during busy operating periods.</li><li>Fridge refusing to start: describe which lights, controls and fans still operate, since that distinction helps the engineer separate a full interruption from a fault affecting only refrigeration.</li><li>Leaking water near the equipment: the drainage arrangement and any ice formation need assessment before the source can be confirmed, particularly with units installed beneath counters or behind displays.</li><li>Repeated noise or vibration: a change in sound may involve fans, contact with surrounding fittings or other moving parts. Record when it happens without opening guarded service areas yourself.</li><li>Doors that will not seal properly: worn gaskets, damaged hinges and alignment issues deserve different remedies, making a full closure check more useful than ordering a seal without inspection.</li><li>Cooling that varies across shelves: product placement and air movement can influence distribution. Explain where staff notice the problem so the investigation can consider the cabinet&#x27;s internal arrangement.</li></ul></div><div class='trust'><div><b>⭐ 500+</b><br>London Businesses</div><div><b>🔧 Same Day</b><br>Fix Rate 92%</div><div><b>📍 All London</b><br>Zones 1-6 Covered</div></div><div class='cta'><h2>LET'S GET IT SORTED 24/7</h2><p>Commercial refrigeration support across London. Call to discuss your fault and arrange an engineer visit.</p><a href='tel:07983759320'>CALL 07983 759320 NOW</a></div><section class="seo-depth pillar" style="max-width:900px;margin:24px auto;padding:0 16px 8px;line-height:1.7">
<h2>Commercial Fridge Repair London - 24/7 Emergency</h2>
<p>Cold Direct is the commercial fridge engineer London sites call when chilled food is drifting above safe holding temperatures. This fridge repair London page is for trade cabinets only: we do not do household repairs and we will not attend a domestic Bosch or Beko in a flat. Emergency fridge repair London runs 24/7 with a typical 60 to 90 minute attendance. Commercial fridge repair London covers prep counters, upright Gastronorm cabinets, back-bar units and display fridges used by restaurants, pubs, takeaways, cafes, shops and hotels. A commercial fridge engineer London tests on site, then prices labour and parts before work starts. Restaurants with warm prep rails, pubs with warm bottled beer, takeaways with rising salad wells, cafes with dairy displays, shops with grab-and-go cases and hotels with breakfast cold rooms all need the same commercial response. We repair Williams, Foster, Polar, True, Blizzard, Gram and Lec catering fridges in restaurants, pubs, takeaways, cafes, shops and hotels. Call 07983 759320 if a commercial fridge in a restaurant, pub, takeaway, cafe, shop or hotel is not holding 1–5°C. Same-day commercial fridge repair London is confirmed on the phone. Keep HACCP probes running; a repaired fridge does not certify dumped stock. We do not do household repairs.</p>
<h2>Common Commercial Fridge Faults We Fix Daily</h2>
<p>A warm fridge in a restaurant, pub or takeaway can dump high-risk food and invite EHO questions if HACCP records show a gap. We find the fault before we quote.</p>
<ul>
<li><strong>Not cooling / warm:</strong> cabinets in restaurants, pubs, takeaways, cafes, shops and hotels that will not recover after service.</li>
<li><strong>Ice build-up:</strong> iced evaporators and blocked drains that starve airflow and push product temperature up.</li>
<li><strong>Compressor failure:</strong> start-relay, capacitor or seized compressors on stainless catering fridges.</li>
<li><strong>Gas leak:</strong> F-Gas leak find and recharge after the joint or pipe is repaired.</li>
<li><strong>Door seal:</strong> failed gaskets that pull kitchen heat into the cabinet and fog glass doors in shops.</li>
<li><strong>Thermostat / controller:</strong> set-point drift, frozen probes and error codes on digital controllers.</li>
<li><strong>Fan motor:</strong> evaporator or condenser fans that stop and overheat the pack.</li>
<li><strong>Blocked condenser:</strong> dust and grease behind takeaway and cafe counters, cleaned and tested first.</li>
</ul>
<p>Stock loss is immediate. HACCP and EHO risk follows if you cannot show holding temperatures. We restore the fridge; you keep food-safety decisions.</p>
